  "source": "book/assets/resource-mediation-stack.svg",
  "claim": "The resource-mediation composition. A RESOURCE POLICY states which resource is scarce and what capacity is acceptable; a MEDIATOR admits at most N actors through one admission point to the SHARED RESOURCE. A dashed LIVE PRESSURE loop tightens or relaxes effective capacity when justified. N=1 and N>1 are settings of the same mediator, not separate stacks. Solid path: the required path. Dashed attachment: a useful enhancement, not required for the capability.",
  "topology": "A solid load-bearing path runs top to bottom. RESOURCE POLICY declares which resource is\n    scarce and what capacity is acceptable. The MEDIATOR routes every access through one admission point,\n    admitting at most N actors. The SHARED RESOURCE sits below it, now governed by explicit policy rather\n    than actor timing. One enhancement attaches as a dashed, open-arrowed feedback: LIVE PRESSURE can tighten\n    or relax the effective capacity when justified, but only after the fixed policy and admission seam exist.\n    N equals one and N greater than one are settings of the same mediator, not separate stacks.",
  "required_terms": [
    "RESOURCE POLICY capacity · scope",
    "MEDIATOR admit ≤ N actors",
    "SHARED RESOURCE",
    "LIVE PRESSURE tighten / relax when justified",
    "N = 1 and N > 1 are settings of the same mediator. Solid: required. Dashed: enhancement."
  ],
